        "id": 1000423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-08-11T20:44:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For most cases it should be possible to have just one mask because the non-relevant events (like EC_HOST_EVENT_MODE_CHANGE) should only end up being seen on a capable device.\n\nBut it might make sense to define a mask of the basic wake events for different categories which can be used by (at least most) boards.  coreboot has a similar issue for our x86 boards, lots of copied around headers with wake masks that are mostly the same but sometimes have a difference that is hard to understand without digging into the commit history.",
      "parentUuid": "082f2a2a_b6af4717",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 188,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "9b285c5ea6d60eb3c6553c8c2bad7719fcc650db",
