      "writtenOn": "2020-08-11T21:18:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for giving the background.\n\nAfter digging into several old bugs and materials, the \"AC insert\" was not a wake source of S3, as Duncan said. And also highlighted \"AC insert must wake EC but not AP\" for the deep sleep mode (EC hibernate).\n\nBut a recent update adds a new rule on the CrOS hardware requirement that includes \"AC plug/unplug\" as a wake source of S3.\nhttps://chrome-internal-review.googlesource.com/c/chromeos/requirements/+/3192377/4/_data/system-performance-and-behavior/wake-table-conv.yml\n\nCrOS hardware requirement:\nhttps://chromeos.google.com/partner/dlm/docs/latest-requirements/convertible.html#wake-sources-and-battery-life\n\nThe update is very new i.e. Aug 7, and should be the source of truth. I will modify this CL to reflect the update.",
      "parentUuid": "c81d4581_0727877e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 188,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 188,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "9b285c5ea6d60eb3c6553c8c2bad7719fcc650db",
